2:T14cd,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Blog","name":"Solar Ireland Blog","description":"Expert solar panel advice for Irish homeowners.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog","inLanguage":"en-IE","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Solar Ireland","url":"https://solarireland.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://solarireland.com/logo-lg.png","width":512,"height":512}},"blogPost":[{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"The Complete Guide to the SEAI Solar Grant in 2026","description":"Everything you need to know about the €1,800 SEAI solar panel grant — eligibility, how to apply, timelines, and how to maximise your savings with the Clean Export Guarantee.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/complete-guide-seai-solar-grant-2026","datePublished":"15 Apr 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"How Much Do Solar Panels Cost in Ireland? (2026 Prices)","description":"A transparent breakdown of solar panel costs in Ireland for 2026 — from 4kWp to 10kWp systems, including installation, grants, and what affects the final price.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/how-much-do-solar-panels-cost-ireland-2026","datePublished":"12 Apr 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Solar Panels in Winter: Do They Actually Work?","description":"A common myth in Ireland is that solar panels are useless in winter. The truth might surprise you — panels still generate 30-50% of their summer output during the darker months.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/solar-panels-in-winter-do-they-work","datePublished":"8 Apr 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Clean Export Guarantee Explained: Get Paid for Your Excess Solar","description":"The Clean Export Guarantee (CEG) allows you to sell surplus solar electricity back to the grid. Here's how it works, what you'll earn, and which suppliers offer the best rates.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/clean-export-guarantee-explained","datePublished":"4 Apr 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"East vs South vs West-Facing Roofs: Which Is Best for Solar?","description":"Does your roof face the right way for solar? We compare east, south and west-facing installations with real Irish data to show which orientation delivers the best returns.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/east-vs-south-vs-west-facing-roofs-solar","datePublished":"28 Mar 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Battery Storage: Is It Worth the Extra Cost?","description":"Solar batteries cost €4,000-€8,000 — but can they pay for themselves? We break down the maths with real Irish energy prices and usage patterns to help you decide.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/battery-storage-is-it-worth-the-extra-cost","datePublished":"22 Mar 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Planning Permission for Solar Panels in Ireland — What You Need to Know","description":"Good news — most domestic solar installations in Ireland don't need planning permission. Here are the exceptions, limits, and guidelines you should be aware of before installing.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/planning-permission-solar-panels-ireland","datePublished":"18 Mar 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"LONGi vs Jinko vs Trina: Which Solar Panels Are Best for Irish Homes?","description":"We compare the top three tier-1 solar panel brands used in Ireland — efficiency, warranties, real-world performance, and which one delivers the best value for your home.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/longi-vs-jinko-vs-trina-best-solar-panels","datePublished":"12 Mar 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Solar Panels in Dublin: The Ultimate 2026 Guide","description":"Everything Dublin homeowners need to know about going solar — from grant eligibility and installation costs to the best panels for Dublin's weather and typical roof types.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/solar-panels-dublin-ultimate-guide","datePublished":"6 Mar 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"},{"@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"SEAI Grant Stays at €1,800 for 2026 — What It Means for You","description":"The government has confirmed the SEAI solar panel grant will remain at €1,800 for 2026. Here is what the announcement means for homeowners, the grant's history, and why now is still the time to apply.","url":"https://solarireland.com/blog/seai-grant-stay-e1800-2026-what-it-means","datePublished":"28 Apr 2026","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cal O'Reilly"},"image":"https://solarireland.com/og-blog.png"}]}0:{"buildId":"_xtFLUnTQfBsxjRlX7tNZ","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[null,[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"CollectionPage\",\"@id\":\"https://solarireland.com/blog\",\"name\":\"Solar Energy Blog\",\"description\":\"Expert solar panel advice for Irish homeowners. SEAI grant guides, cost breakdowns, savings calculators, and installation tips.\",\"url\":\"https://solarireland.com/blog\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-IE\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://solarireland.com/#website\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://solarireland.com/#organization\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\